{"start":"<h2>First, find somewhere worth looking.</h2><p>Qwen orders source files by how well their text matches the issue. Rank 1 is its first suggestion; rank 28 means 27 files come before it. A rank is a position, not a confidence score.</p><!--StartFacts--><p>The optional graph at the end shows this retained neighborhood, not the whole repository.</p><p>Finding one relevant file is useful. It does not mean we found the whole fix.</p>","connections":"<h2>What makes this a matching pattern?</h2><p>A connection is a recorded fact. A structural pattern is a small set of facts that fit together. A design-pattern name still needs evidence from the source.</p><!--ConnectionFacts-->","source":"<h2>Check what the connection actually means.</h2><p>A graph tells us that code is connected. The source tells us what those connections do.</p><!--SourceFacts-->","results":"<h2>Did we find every file the fix needed?</h2><p>The three saved conditions use the same candidate files. Q is Qwen’s original order. QJ is Jev’s judgment of the original first 32; QS is a separate judgment of those same 32, with Atlas clues. QS does not run after QJ.</p><p>Positions 1 through 10 count as recovered at this cutoff. A larger rank means the file is farther down the list, not absent from the repository. Finding one required file is an any-file hit. Finding every eligible required file is a complete recovery.</p><!--ResultFacts--><p>A rank change is an observation, not an explanation of the model’s reasoning. Structure supplied metadata to Jev. It did not independently decide these ranks.</p>","theory":"<h2>Why this stays small</h2><p>There are three different limits here: <strong>the size of a structural question</strong>, <strong>the number of question descriptions</strong>, and <strong>the number of files Jev judges</strong>. None is a bound on the size of the repository or the number of matching answers.</p><p>The code below is the current Flix implementation, copied with its original comments and line numbers. It explains the machinery; it does not establish which implementation produced the frozen benchmark results.</p><h3>A question can mention only a few connections</h3><p>An <em>atom</em> is one relation, such as Imports. A <em>role</em> is a numbered place for a file or symbol. An <em>output</em> is a place whose value should be returned.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/bounds.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:100–122</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"100\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on positive binary atoms.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"101\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxAtoms</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">3</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"102\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"103\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on typed role slots.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"104\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxRoles</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">4</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"105\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"106\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on projected output slots.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"107\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxOutputs</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">2</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"108\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"109\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on bound inequalities.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"110\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxInequalities</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"111\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"112\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on consistent role renamings canonicalization may use.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"113\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxRenamings</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">24</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"114\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"115\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on canonical candidates in one deterministic population.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"116\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxCandidates</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">256</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"117\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"118\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared starting shard granularity.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"119\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">shardSize</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">32</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"120\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"121\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The declared bound on theory shards per world.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"122\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxShards</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">8</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>Read the first four limits as: <strong>at most three connections, four places, two returned values and one “these must differ” condition</strong>. The three-step file → function → function → file example fits exactly.</p><p>The built-in template family declares one- and two-atom descriptions. The grammar can admit three atoms; that does not mean every admitted three-atom description is in the default family.</p><h3>The limit is checked before matching</h3><p><code>safe</code> reads a description and returns a Boolean. It checks the number of atoms, that they connect, that their types agree, and that each requested output actually appears in the question.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/safe.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:224–243</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"224\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// True exactly when the descriptor is inside the admitted grammar.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"225\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">safe</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Bool</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"226\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> atoms = candidate#atoms;</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"227\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> count = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"228\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        count &gt;= </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> and count &lt;= </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxAtoms</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"229\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">forAll</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(slotInRange, </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">roleList</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms))</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"230\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">forAll</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom -&gt; atom#subject != atom#object, atoms)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"231\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">connected</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"232\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsConsistent</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"233\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#outputs) &gt;= </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"234\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#outputs) &lt;= </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxOutputs</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"235\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">distinct</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#outputs)) == </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#outputs)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"236\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">forAll</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(output -&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">bound</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(output, atoms), candidate#outputs)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"237\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#denied) &lt;= </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxInequalities</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"238\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            and </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">forAll</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(pair -&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">match</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> pair {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"239\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">                </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">case</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (left, right) =&gt; left != right and </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">bound</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(left, atoms) and </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">bound</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(right, atoms)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"240\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            }, candidate#denied)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"241\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"242\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"243\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">slotInRange</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(slot: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Bool</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = slot &gt;= </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">0</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> and slot &lt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxRoles</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span></code></pre></figure><p><code>bound(output, atoms)</code> means the requested output slot occurs in the facts being matched. The final check applies the same rule to both sides of an inequality. A malformed question is refused instead of acquiring an invented endpoint.</p><h3>A file cannot silently become a function</h3><p>For every role, <code>domainsConsistent</code> gathers the domains required by its relations. After removing duplicates, there can be no more than one domain for that role.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/domains.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:275–285</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"275\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// One role slot must mean one nominal domain. The domains come from the core</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"276\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// signature table, so an atom that reads a role as a file and an atom that</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"277\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// writes it as a symbol cannot be composed into one conjunction.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"278\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsConsistent</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">AtomPattern</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">]): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Bool</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"279\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">forAll</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(role -&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">distinct</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsOf</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(role, atoms))) &lt;= </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">distinct</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">roleList</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms)))</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"280\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"281\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsOf</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(role: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, atoms: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">AtomPattern</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">]): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Domain</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">] =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"282\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">flatMap</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom -&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"283\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            (</span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (atom#subject == role) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Attune</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">atomSource</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom#relation) :: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"284\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">                ::: (</span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (atom#object == role) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Attune</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">atomTarget</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom#relation) :: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">),</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"285\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            atoms)</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>So <code>Defines ; Calls</code> can connect: Defines ends at a Symbol and Calls starts at a Symbol. <code>Imports ; Calls</code> cannot connect directly: its middle place would need to be both a File and a Symbol.</p><h3>Different slot names should not create duplicate questions</h3><p>Renaming the slots in the same description should not multiply the work. <code>canonical</code> chooses one stable representation. <code>identityKey</code> turns that representation into its identity.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/canonical.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:302–313</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"302\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The canonical descriptor: the least of the consistent renamings, with the</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"303\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// atoms sorted and de-duplicated and the roles renumbered by first</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"304\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// appearance.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"305\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">canonical</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"306\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">match</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">bestOption</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate, </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">renamings</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(), </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">None</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"307\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">case</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">None</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">         =&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">emptyDescriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"308\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">case</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Some</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(option) =&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">renumber</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">renamed</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate, option))</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"309\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        }</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"310\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"311\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The canonical identity key. Two descriptors share it exactly when they are</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"312\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// the same candidate up to a consistent renaming of their role slots.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"313\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">identityKey</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">String</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">render</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">canonical</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate))</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>This is a structural identity. It is not a label such as “plugin system,” and it does not say that two repositories behave the same way.</p><h3>Keep a bounded population of descriptions</h3><p><code>population</code> resolves duplicate IDs, canonicalizes descriptions, rejects unsafe ones, removes equivalent descriptions, and keeps a deterministic prefix.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/population.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:479–496</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"479\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The deterministic bounded population: unsafe descriptors and duplicates</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"480\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// removed, one descriptor per candidate id, sorted by canonical identity.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"481\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">population</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidates: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Candidate</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">]): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Population</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"482\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> ordered = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">sortBy</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate -&gt; candidate#id, candidates);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"483\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (conflicts, unique) = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">resolveIds</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(ordered, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"484\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> canonicalCandidates = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">map</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate -&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"485\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            { id = candidate#id, descriptor = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">canonical</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#descriptor) }, unique);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"486\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> admitted = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">filter</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate -&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">safe</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#descriptor), canonicalCandidates);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"487\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> distinct = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">dedupIdentities</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(admitted, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"488\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> kept = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">sortBy</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate -&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">identityKey</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate#descriptor), distinct);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"489\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> bounded = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">take</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxCandidates</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(), kept);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"490\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"491\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            kept = bounded,</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"492\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            dropped = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidates) - </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(bounded),</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"493\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            conflicts = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">reverse</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(conflicts),</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"494\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            truncated = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(kept) &gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxCandidates</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"495\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        }</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"496\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    }</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>The limit of <strong>256 candidates here means 256 structural descriptions</strong>, not 256 source files. The returned <code>dropped</code>, <code>conflicts</code> and <code>truncated</code> fields preserve what was excluded.</p><p>The kept descriptions are divided into batches. This bounds the description work scheduled per batch; it does not cap the number of matching rows.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/shards.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:532–538</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"532\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// Split one population into world-level shards at the declared granularity.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"533\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">shards</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(population: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Population</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Shards</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"534\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> all = </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">isEmpty</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(population#kept)) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">chunks</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">shardSize</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(), population#kept);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"535\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> bounded = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">take</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxShards</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(), all);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"536\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> total = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">foldLeft</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">((count, shard) -&gt; count + </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(shard), </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">0</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, bounded);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"537\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        { shards = bounded, dropped = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(population#kept) - total, truncated = </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(all) &gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">maxShards</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">() }</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"538\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    }</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>Theory’s batch size of 32 and Jev’s top-32 file window are separate limits on different things. Their equal number does not make them the same population.</p><h3>Reuse a match when the starting point changes</h3><p>A <code>Binding</code> contains the matched entities. <code>Output</code> selects the requested slots. <code>Task</code> joins those existing results to an <code>Anchor</code>, the application’s chosen starting entity, in the same source snapshot.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/reuse.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:911–918</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"911\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">// shape projection: the two declared output slots of one binding.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"912\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Output</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(c, w, </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">role</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(out0, e0, e1, e2, e3), </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">role</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(out1, e0, e1, e2, e3)) :-</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"913\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Binding</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(c, w, e0, e1, e2, e3),</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"914\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Desc</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(c, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, out0, out1).</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"915\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"916\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">// anchored application join: a task or pair context joins an anchor to an</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"917\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">// already materialized structural row and never re-evaluates the structure.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"918\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Task</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(c, w, x, y) :- </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Output</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(c, w, x, y), </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Anchor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(w, x).</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>Read the last rule as: <strong>keep this matched pair when its first entity is the chosen anchor</strong>. The anchor join uses already materialized structural rows; it does not rerun structural matching for that join.</p><!--TheoryFacts--><h3>Keep model judgment narrow too</h3><p>The frozen study asks Jev about Qwen’s first 32 files. The promotion rule puts Relevant decisions first, then uses the original rank to keep the order stable.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/promotion.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Study/Jev.flix:56–61</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"56\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// Whether an outcome promotes its candidate. Only `Relevant` does.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"57\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">promotes</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(outcome: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">JevOutcome</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Bool</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = outcome == </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">JevOutcome</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Relevant</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"58\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"59\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The frozen stable promotion key `(Relevant ? 0 : 1, original base rank)`.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"60\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">promotionKey</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(outcome: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">JevOutcome</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, baseRank: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): (</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">) =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"61\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        (</span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">promotes</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(outcome)) </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">0</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, baseRank)</span></span></code></pre></figure><p>This code orders the decisions; it does not impose the top-32 request window itself. That window comes from the study setup. A required file below Q32 cannot be rescued by this promotion.</p><h3>What “small” does not promise</h3><p>A short question can still match many files around a popular helper. A large source world can still require substantial extraction and matching work. Embedding retrieval also has its own cost.</p><p>The design bounds descriptions and narrows judgment. <strong>The census does not measure latency, memory, tokens or dollars</strong>, so these mechanisms are not a benchmark of cheap execution.</p>"}